+EE-delta action chunk of length 50"), and the shipped norm stats prove it:
+`scripts/compute_norm_stats.py` runs *after* `data_transforms.inputs`, and the
+action stats are per-step-sized (z mean −0.0011, std 0.0044, q99 0.0101) rather
+than up-to-50-step chunk displacements, while state z mean is 1.3924. So use
+`--action-space delta` (cumsum) — the `VLAPolicy` default.
+
+**We initially got this wrong.** Deriving `pi0_gate` from `pi0_libero` dragged
+in LIBERO's `DeltaActions`/`AbsoluteActions` push, so the output chain ran
+`Unnormalize → AbsoluteActions → LiberoOutputs` and added the raw state to
+every row. Symptoms:
+
+- action col 2 (z) came back ≈ 1.5291–1.5328 at drone altitude 1.5 m — a
+  state-sized *offset* with a delta-sized *spread* (0.0037 ≈ the 0.0044 z std);
+- `delta` mode then exploded geometrically: 50 rows × ~1.53 m ⇒ z 1.5 → 76.6 →
+  3983 → …  (the observed chunk-0 cumsum was exactly 76.571);
+- `absolute` mode papered over it, because re-anchoring subtracts row 0 and
+  cancels the constant state offset — but that also cancels the real motion
+  (`abs[k] − abs[0]` = `delta[k] − delta[0]` ≈ 0), which is why "honest
+  re-anchored integration" made the policy look like it barely moved.
+
+`_GateDataConfig` in the patch removes the push. Verify with:
+
+```bash
+env -u VIRTUAL_ENV XLA_PYTHON_CLIENT_PREALLOCATE=false \
+    ~/code/openpi/.venv/bin/python tools/gate_pi0/probe_action_space.py \
